<title>NEW ZEALAND: TransAlta NZ lists at NZ$1.55.</title>
<headline>TransAlta NZ lists at NZ$1.55.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransAlta New Zealand Ltd, formed from the merger of Wellington power companies EnergyDirect and Capital Power, listed on the New Zealand Stock Exchange on Monday at NZ$1.55.  </p>
<p>The shares traded up to $1.65 in early business on volume of 37,000.</p>
<p>TransAlta Corp of Canada, which owned 41 percent of EnergyDirect and all of Capital Power, has a 63 percent interest in the merged company.</p>
<p>TransAlta NZ is New Zealand's fourth largest electricity supply company.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
